Lab 6: Notifications and Slack Integration
-------------------
Areas Covered

Notification in Jenkins.
Integration of Slack tool with Jenkins.
Setup Slack workspace and channel.
Slack plugin and configuration in Jenkins.
Slack integration in pipelines.
Running Jenkins job from Slack slash commands.
------------------------

Requirements

Slack workspace with a channel (e.g., #jenkins-alerts).
Slack Notification plugin.
--------------------------

Plan of Execution and Guidance

Slack Setup:
Create app at api.slack.com > Add to workspace > Bot token scopes: chat:write, commands.
Channel: Invite bot.
Production Tip: Use incoming webhooks for simple alerts; OAuth for interactive commands.
Jenkins Configuration:
Manage Jenkins > Configure System > Slack > Add token and channel.
Test Connection.
-------------------

Integrate in Pipeline:
Post-build: slackSend channel: '#jenkins-alerts', message: "Build ${currentBuild.result}".
---------------------

Slash Commands:
Slack app > Enable Slash Commands > Request URL: <jenkins-url>/slack/notifications.
In pipeline: Use slackin for interactive responses.
Guidance: Trigger job: /jenkins build First-Pipeline.Production Tip: Rate-limit notifications; use colors (good=green, failure=red) for visual alerts.
------------------------
Solution

Expected Outcome: Build success sends green message to Slack; failure red. Slash command triggers job.
-------------------------
Pipeline Snippet:groovy
post {
    success { slackSend color: 'good', message: "Success: $$ {env.JOB_NAME} # $${env.BUILD_NUMBER}" }
    failure { slackSend color: 'danger', message: "Failed: $$ {env.JOB_NAME} # $${env.BUILD_NUMBER} (<${env.BUILD_URL}|View>)" }
}
--------------------------
Verification: Slack channel shows message with build link. Command: /jenkins build Maven-Java-Build > Job queues.
Production Guideline: Archive notifications in centralized logging (ELK stack); avoid sensitive data in messages.
